tents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adjectives to Describe Food"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Food is also a good way to introduce people to a new culture. There are many specific adjectives to describe how food tastes."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Describing Food\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Definition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Flavors\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sweet<br> Salty<br> Bitter<br> Smoky<br> Hot/Spicy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A sugary flavor<br> Tastes too much of salt<br> Strong or unpleasant flavor<br> The taste of smoked wood<br> To make one's mouth burn\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Textures\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Creamy<br> Crunchy<br> Greasy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Smooth, soft and thick<br> A hard texture<br> Tastes of oil\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This burger has a smoky flavor."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This Indian curry is so spicy."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This ice-cream is so rich and creamy."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to proofread"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to read and correct written mistakes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Proofread your work as well when you are done."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use in a paragraph about food."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bland"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not interesting or exciting"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:The mild ones were too bland."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "comma"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a punctuation mark , that you use to separate words or groups of words in a sentence"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Capital letters, periods, commas and question marks are very important."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spread"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large meal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was such a big spread of food at the party."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "buffet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a meal for which different foods are placed on a table so that people can serve themselves"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We had an Indian buffet dinner."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le07ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le07ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pronouns One vs. Ones"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the pronouns <span class = \"strong\">one</span> (singular) and <span class = \"strong\">ones</span> (plural) to replace nouns. You often use demonstratives (<span class=\"italic\">this, that, these, those</span>) with <span class=\"italic\">one</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ones</span>.<br/><br/>Example: <span class = \"italic\">There are two pies. I like <span class = \"strong\">this one</span>. It's an apple pie.</span><br/><br/>You can use them after <span class = \"italic\">Which</span> in questions.<br/><br/>Example:<span class = \"italic\"> Which one</span>? or <span class = \"italic\">Which ones</span>?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interview a friend or family member about their favorite restaurant."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask 5 questions about the different dishes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the answers to write a paragraph about their favorite restaurant."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the paragraph aloud. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I ask questions about food."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a paragraph about food."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the paragraph to share my information."}]}], "type": "sena"}